        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nPR #88082 added `step-3.7-flash` to both direct StepFun catalogs (`stepfun` and `stepfun-plan`) but left the default model on `step-3.5-flash`. New onboarding runs and catalog defaults still select the older Step 3.5 model instead of the current flagship.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\n`STEPFUN_DEFAULT_MODEL_ID` is the single source for both `STEPFUN_DEFAULT_MODEL_REF` and `STEPFUN_PLAN_DEFAULT_MODEL_REF`. Those refs drive `onboard.ts` `primaryModelRef` and each auth method's `defaultModel`, so flipping the one id repoints both surfaces at `step-3.7-flash` with no other runtime wiring.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\n- Fresh StepFun onboarding (standard and Step Plan) now defaults to `stepfun/step-3.7-flash` / `stepfun-plan/step-3.7-flash`.\r\n- Existing installs that pinned a model explicitly are unaffected; the change only moves the default for new setups.\r\n- `step-3.5-flash` and `step-3.5-flash-2603` remain selectable.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n- `extensions/stepfun/provider-catalog.ts`: `STEPFUN_DEFAULT_MODEL_ID` now `step-3.7-flash`.\r\n- Updated `extensions/stepfun/index.test.ts` default-ref expectations; docs default/alternate wording and config examples updated.\r\n- Local proof (Codex worktree fallback):\r\n  - `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check docs/providers/stepfun.md extensions/stepfun/index.test.ts extensions/stepfun/provider-catalog.ts` — clean.\r\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/stepfun/index.test.ts src/agents/models-config.providers.stepfun.test.ts` — 6 tests passed across 2 shards.\r\n\n\n## Fresh-onboarding behavior proof\n\nDrove the real StepFun onboard preset appliers (the functions the setup wizard invokes: `applyStepFunStandardConfig`, `applyStepFunStandardConfigCn`, `applyStepFunPlanConfig`, `applyStepFunPlanConfigCn`) against a fresh empty config. All four fresh auth choices select `step-3.7-flash`:\n\n| Setup                           | `agents.defaults.model.primary` |\n|---------------------------------|---------------------------------|\n| Standard API key (Global/Intl)  | `stepfun/step-3.7-flash`        |\n| Standard API key (China)        | `stepfun/step-3.7-flash`        |\n| Step Plan API key (Global/Intl) | `stepfun-plan/step-3.7-flash`   |\n| Step Plan API key (China)       | `stepfun-plan/step-3.7-flash`   |\n\nSingle shared constant `STEPFUN_DEFAULT_MODEL_ID` repoints both products. Full `openclaw onboard` CLI terminal output was not captured because the local sandbox blocks the package mirror; the appliers above are the exact code the wizard runs to set the primary model.\n",
